Build a small playable browser game inspired by Rocket League: drive a car, boost, hit the ball into the opponent goal, show clear scoring feedback, and support reset/restart. Use real Rocket League screenshots or gameplay as the visual reference; choose one concrete reference and justify it in one sentence. The lead should choose the approach and split the goal into the smallest independently judgeable pieces. For each important piece, use a separate builder and a fresh-context critic who inspects the actual output, compares it directly with the reference (blind A/B where practical), identifies the largest remaining gap, and sends it back for improvement until it reaches the bar or the run is stopped. Maintain a simple live progress page.
